WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.400
If you’re anything like me,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.560
you have lots of ambitious
plans for the future.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.160
I’ve got a whole series of
new books I want to write,

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.400
thousands more
videos to script.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.360
But guess what?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.760
None of us may be able to do
any of the things we want to do

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.240
if we don't have our health.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.480
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.960
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.960
Just ate some garlicky hummus?

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.560
Great! But you may want to
listen in on our first story.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.080
Approximately
one in three people

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.240
suffer from halitosis-
bad breath.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.360
What can we do about it?

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.840
I've got videos
on tongue cleaning, gum chewing,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.360
and the best mouthwash.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.240
Population studies suggest
that those who eat

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.160
fewer fruits and vegetables
may be at higher risk,

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.960
but there are a lot of things
associated with worse diets

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.040
that are also linked
to halitosis,

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.160
though the fruit
and vegetable link

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.080
seemed to remain
even after controlling

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:58.320
for these other factors.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.160
It works in dogs.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.400
Vegetable chew toys
seem to help,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.240
but what about people?

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.280
There's a compound found
in cruciferous vegetables

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.560
that can effectively eliminate
the volatile sulfur compounds

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.000
like the rotten egg gas
hydrogen sulfide.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.720
These are the foul gases
that cause bad breath

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.240
produced mainly
from the breakdown

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.920
of sulfur-containing
amino acids

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.200
concentrated in animal protein-
cysteine and methionine.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.640
The cruciferous compound gloms
onto the sulfur compound

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.720
and prevents it
from going gaseous;

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.800
whereas peppermint,
spearmint, wintergreen,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.280
and many of the flavors
in breath mints and chewing gum

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.800
didn't actually treat the cause,

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.200
and just kind of have
a masking effect.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.160
Whereas something
like broccoli chewing gum

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.080
might help
at least temporarily,

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.520
but why not just eat broccoli
instead?

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.360
Researchers have tried
using a compound

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.280
that clears cysteine
from the tongue

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.480
for those who don't just want
to try to cut down on casein

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:55.000
and other animal proteins
that are concentrated in it.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.720
The compound they used
is derived from kiwi fruit,

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.840
so can you just eat kiwis
instead?

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:01.920
No word on halitosis,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.600
but twice daily kiwi fruit
consumption for two months

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.040
showed significant improvements
in gingivitis, plaque,

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.440
and gum disease.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.320
Of course, not all fruits
are going to be beneficial.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.280
Durian fruit may give rise
to the most profound bad breath

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.560
because the fruit itself
stinks to high heaven,

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.800
as many of you will remember

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.920
from my harrowing experience
with it in medical school

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.720
that I sheepishly related
in my book How Not to Die.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.920
And the vegetable
that comes to mind

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.240
when you think bad breath
is garlic.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.760
Is there anything you can do
to deodorize garlic breath

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.160
using different kinds of foods?

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:43.680
Well, you don't know
until you put it to the test.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.320
After giving people
some garlic,

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.920
they tried whey protein,
lemon juice, green tea,

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:50.840
chlorophyll, 7UP soda,
a raw pink lady apple,

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:54.120
a cooked apple, parsley,
spinach, and mint leaves.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.360
Anyone want to take a guess
as to which worked best?

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:01.320
Parsley, spinach,
and mint treatments

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.360
were effective
in the deodorization

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.440
of garlic breath
stinky compounds.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:09.040
They're all green,
so they wondered

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.360
if it was the chlorophyll,
and it turned out, nope,

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.380
chlorophyll alone didn't help.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.720
There are four
stinky garlic compounds.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.600
If you don't do anything
after the garlic,

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.840
the stench goes away
on its own.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.880
And taking chlorophyll didn't
seem to change that at all,

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.680
but parsley, spinach,
and mint did,

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.600
starting almost immediately.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.400
What do we think was going on?

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.880
Well, raw apples worked better
than cooked apples,

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.760
which are basically
the same food

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.680
except for the enzymes
being destroyed by heating,

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:40.160
so maybe there's
some enzymatic deodorization.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.440
Here's the data.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.280
And, yes, raw worked better
than cooked,

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.040
but cooked still worked
better than nothing,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.320
and so did the lemon juice
and green tea,

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.160
even though they didn't have
any active enzymes

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.280
since they were
both pasteurized.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.240
Here's the beverages data.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.000
The whey protein in water
didn't seem to help at all,

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.160
even compared with the soda,

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.680
though green tea and lemon
appeared to do better.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.720
Maybe the acidic pH

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.400
was involved
in the deodorization

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.160
from the lemon juice

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.080
and soft drink
breath experiments,

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.600
since they used
a sour lemon-lime soft drink.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:17.360
Garlic breath volatiles
(allyl methyl disulfide,

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.280
diallyl disulfide,
allyl mercaptan)

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.760
were significantly reduced
by parsley, spinach, mint,

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:26.480
raw and microwaved apple,
soft drink, green tea,

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.560
and lemon juice treatments

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.800
in comparison to water
(the control)

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.640
but were not reduced
by chlorophyll

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.480
and whey protein treatments.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:35.400
And perhaps
the polyphenol phytonutrients

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.800
were the active ingredient
in green tea.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.480
With consumption
of full-flavor garlic,

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.040
it is not yet possible
to completely avoid

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:46.120
malodorous breath associated
with garlic consumption,

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:47.840
but there are some chasers

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.280
that may help you
bring it down a notch.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:51.960
Finally today,

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:58.120
we explore the wondrous properties
of green tea for controlling halitosis.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:01.640
Tea is the second most widely
consumed beverage in the world,

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:05.703
after water, to the tune of
billions of pounds every year.

00:05:05.703 --> 00:05:07.400
In my last video I showed
how drinking green tea

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.760
after eating garlic
helps deodorize your breath.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.200
But what about drinking
green tea

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.640
to deodorize regular bad breath
without the garlic?

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.720
There's been a lot of studies
on the effect of green tea

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:19.280
on other aspects
of oral health.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.440
For example, green tea
appears to work as well

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.720
as chlorhexidine
for reducing plaque,

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:26.120
and chlorhexidine
is like the gold standard.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.120
Green tea is safer too.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.600
Chlorhexidine has
so many side effects

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.400
you're not supposed to use

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.560
if for more than
a short time period;

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.680
side effects like discoloration
of the teeth,

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.200
increased formation of tartar,

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.040
an impairment
of taste sensation,

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.240
and occasionally damage

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.000
to the inner lining
of your mouth,

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.760
whereas if anything,
drinking green tea

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:46.920
appears to have
good side effects.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:50.200
Tea consumption is associated
with living a longer life

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.600
thanks to links
to less cardiac death,

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.960
heart disease, stroke,
and type 2 diabetes-

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.640
and not just by a little.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.160
A three cup (720 ml)
a day increase

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:00.120
in tea consumption per day

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.600
is associated with
a 24 percent decreased risk

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.560
of premature death
from all causes put together,

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.800
the equivalent of adding
about two years

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.640
onto your lifespan.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:13.440
The longevity link extends
to both green tea and black,

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.800
though the per cup effect
appears greater with green.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.680
If you compare
the anti-microbial efficacy

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.000
of green tea and chlorhexidine
mouth rinses

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.360
against the bacteria
associated with tooth decay

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.920
in children with severe
early childhood cavities,

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.640
this study found
that a green tea mouth rinse

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.240
was superior to chlorhexidine,

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.240
but this study
found the opposite.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.800
Chlorhexidine wiped out
like 95 percent

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:38.840
of the decay bacteria,

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:41.480
versus more like 70 percent
for green tea,

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.800
but just rinsing
with water alone

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:45.680
can cut levels in half.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:47.680
So, in terms of
protecting teeth,

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.480
the effectiveness of green tea
as a mouth rinse agent

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:51.440
has not been proven.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:54.320
But what about for bad breath?

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:56.040
The effect of green tea
on halitosis

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.600
has evidently been well known
from early times,

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.920
perhaps due
to the deodorizing activity

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.360
of certain
antioxidant polyphenols.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:08.280
But you don't really know
until you put it to the test.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.160
This study found that sucking
on green tea tablets

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.640
reduced stinky breath compounds,

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:15.860
but who sucks on tea tablets?

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.760
Here, green tea was compared
to breath mints, chewing gum,

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:21.680
and parsley oil,
and green tea seemed to help,

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:24.320
but did not reach
statistical significance.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:27.440
But again, it wasn't drinking
or swishing with green tea,

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:29.720
but rather
some green tea powder

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.360
sprinkled on people's tongues.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:35.000
This study used actual tea

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.840
and found
that one minute later,

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.360
swishing with green tea
was no better

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.520
than swishing with water.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.600
Okay, but what about chronic use
over time?

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:48.040
This is the study
I had been looking for.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.800
A randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.680
in which people
rinsed their mouths twice a day

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.680
for a month
with a green tea mouthwash

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.480
or a similar looking/tasting
placebo mouthwash.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.120
And at the end of the month,

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:04.760
the stinky bad breath compounds
were reduced nearly 40 percent

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:08.320
in the green tea group versus
closer to only 10 percent

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.240
in the placebo group.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.840
Bottom line:
a systematic review

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.360
on the effect of the tea plant

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.840
on decreasing
the level of halitosis

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.520
concluded
that green tea mouthwash

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:20.240
can indeed reduce bad breath,

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:21.520
though they don't feel
the evidence

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.760
is sufficiently robust
for dentists

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:25.800
to start recommending it
on its own

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:28.960
due to lack of enough
randomized clinical studies.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:31.760
But green tea mouthwash can be
a good treatment of choice

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.560
beside other halitosis
treatments,

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:34.640
like tongue scraping,

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:37.800
to achieve
better clinical results.

